224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>This morning, I lived a moment of magic.  It was only light, and only for moments. It was enough to let me know, it's there, waiting for us.  It is waiting for us to know that magic, light, and hope for the future are all within our grasp.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1092\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1092,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1988861,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BijS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F51d6e334-8963-4040-8873-b27b7b1f29e2_4032x3024.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The moment can pass.  Don't let it be forgotten.</p><p>I'm going to end this article, such as it were, this song, written about living in here, in Brooklyn.</p><iframe class=\"spotify-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;image&quot;:&quot;https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b2737e83a2bfb02b405cbba36974&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Hurricane of Me&quot;,&quot;subtitle&quot;:&quot;Owen Muir&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.spotify.com/track/2bssHEOO7aC8zNuOki6TTa&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;noScroll&quot;:false}\" src=\"https://open.spotify.com/embed/track/2bssHEOO7aC8zNuOki6TTa\" frameborder=\"0\" gesture=\"media\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" allow=\"encrypted-media\" loading=\"lazy\" data-component-name=\"Spotify2ToDOM\"></iframe><p>Thanks for reading, and I hope this Sunday pallet cleanser has been up your alley.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share The Frontier Psychiatrists </span></a></p><p></p><p><br></p>","text":"I have a great view for my apartment. I spent too much time working, and not enough time frolicking around in great views, but that's what it is. I do get to see New York in the morning, and in the evening, and it can be very beautiful.\n\nI was struck this morning, when my eyes opened, to see the following.\n\nI wasn't quite sure what to do about the dark cloud, was it smoke? We had had the Canadian fire last summer, blocking out all the light. That orange light, like dust, happening at dawn. It was a little bit of magic. It only lasted for about two minutes.\n\nSubscribe now\n\nTo give you a sense, here is what that view look like during the fires…\n\nAnd 10 minutes later, on the same day, it looked even worse:\n\nSometimes, we need a reminder that there is magic out there, no matter what we think, no matter what we do. The night, it often sparkles in a way that would be hard to imagine had I not lived in this remarkable now .\n\nThis morning, I lived a moment of magic. It was only light, and only for moments. It was enough to let me know, it's there, waiting for us. It is waiting for us to know that magic, light, and hope for the future are all within our grasp.\n\nThe moment can pass. Don't let it be forgotten.\n\nI'm going to end this article, such as it were, this song, written about living in here, in Brooklyn.\n\nThanks for reading, and I hope this Sunday pallet cleanser has been up your alley.\n\nShare The Frontier Psychiatrists"}